ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: No production team needs session-phase-adaptive draft length. The only regime where adaptive shows a gain (+7–9%) is extreme drift (gap=±0.30, one phase at ~95% acceptance dominating ~55% of a long session) with zero detection error and zero switching tax — a condition the packet explicitly marks “not the realistic operating point” (packet L0 RESULTS). In the realistic deep-session mix (prose/tool/mixed = .25/.55/.20) with p_err>0 and s>0, adaptive loses −2.2% mean net tok/s vs best-tuned-fixed, which already captures ~93% median of the theoretical adaptive gain.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only artifact. The L0 analytic+sim sweep (3,024 configs) shows a broad concave plateau for net-tok/s-vs-k; the session-weighted single k* lands inside every phase’s near-optimum (Jensen floor). With realistic phase-detection error + switching tax, adaptive underperforms the tuned-fixed baseline at the realistic operating point (mean −2.2%, median −2.0%; 4.0% of configs gain >3%). The claimed “material drift” (k_opt 1→15) does not translate to a throughput win in production.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Phase-detection accuracy cost (p_err) and switching/recompile tax (s) turn the theoretical +1.9% ceiling into a −2.2% net loss; Implementation complexity of a cheap-but-reliable context-phase signal for long agentic sessions; Tuning burden already solved by a single best-tuned fixed k (captures 92.7% median with overhead, 80.4% of configs ≥80% captured); Prior-art saturation — EAGLE/EAGLE-2/Medusa/SpecDec++/Dynamic-Speculation-Lookahead already publish draft-length adaptation, removing novelty; Extreme-drift regime (a_tool 0.95 vs a_prose 0.65) not observed in production traces; Negative ROI: added system surface area for ≤0.78% p90 upside at realistic overhead]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 KEY FINDINGS (B): “a single best-tuned fixed k captures ~93% MEDIAN of the adaptive gain at the realistic deep-session mix… With realistic phase-detection error + switching tax, adaptive LOSES -2.2% net tok/s at the realistic operating point. Adaptive reaches +7-9% ONLY under extreme drift… AND zero overhead — and even there tuned-fixed captures ~85%.” Table (B) shows realistic_deep WITH overhead: mean −2.22% / median −2.00% / p90 +0.78%, fixed_captured_frac 0.927. Prior-art caveat: “Draft-length adaptation is PUBLISHED: EAGLE / EAGLE-2 / Medusa / SpecDec++ / Dynamic-Speculation-Lookahead… The only candidate novelty here was the session-phase-drift framing… It does not [beat best-tuned-fixed], so there is no defensible contribution beyond confirming the Jensen floor in yet another setting.” Mechanism: “net tok/s as a function of k is a broad, concave plateau… The plateaus overlap heavily unless acceptances are pathologically far apart. That overlap is the Jensen floor — the same geometry that killed EXP-0006 and EXP-0011.”
```
